  "details": "I'm trying to extend the keyboard from \"Tell Your Word\" by Kanata and found there's no sensible way to manipulate strings within the SDK, so keystrokes are sent to the webpanel instead.\n\nPlease be sure Node Graph includes at least a couple of these:\n\nConcatenation\nJoining (i.e. take an array of strings and put them together with a separator)\nSlicing (aka substrings)\nUpper / lower case\n\nTemplating (i.e. \"foo {input} baz\", with input bar gives \"foo bar baz\")\n\nRegex replacements (for example escaping special characters)\n\nRegex pattern and group matching (for example to grab a youtube video ID out of a link, but only if it's a youtube link)\n\nDecoding and Encoding some important formats. Like HTML entities (UI text could use this for example) and URL parameters (for web panels).\n\nSome predefined character sets to validate against:\nAlphanumerical, ASCII, etc.\n\nI'm sure I'm still forgetting a few.",
